                <h2>Efficient Airflow for Industrial and HVAC Systems</h2>
                <p>Backward Inclined Centrifugal Fans are designed for applications that require reliable airflow with medium to high static pressure. Their blades curve backward against the path of rotation, which helps efficient air movement and makes this design appropriate for many industrial and HVAC systems.</p>
                <p>These fans can handle different ventilation requirements while retaining a practical and robust construction. Selection depends on airflow, static pressure, operating conditions, installation area, and the requirements of the connected system. The right configuration can support stable performance and reliable air movement.</p>
